,"lead":"Underborrowing relative to forecast could signal capital programme slippage or reduced ambition, or prudent cash management; coupled with financing costs doubling, it suggests interest rates on new or refinanced debt were significantly higher than forecast","iso":"2026-09-30","paper_title":"Appendix 2 - Prudential and Treasury Management Indicators 2025/26","paper_url":"https://democracy.gedling.gov.uk/documents/s45873/45873.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Financing costs ratio doubled from 2.21% to 4.62%, showing sharp deterioration in debt affordability","lead":"Lenders use this ratio to assess whether a council's revenue can sustain its debt service; a near-doubling indicates debt service is now consuming much more revenue headroom, leaving less capacity to absorb financial shocks","iso":"2026-09-30","paper_title":"Appendix 2 - Prudential and Treasury Management Indicators 2025/26","paper_url":"https://democracy.gedling.gov.uk/documents/s45873/45873.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-30","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Appendix 2 - Prudential and Treasury Management Indicators 2025/26","paper_url":"https://democracy.gedling.gov.uk/documents/s45873/45873.pdf","headline":"Entire borrowing portfolio concentrated in long-term: 94% over 10 years, zero borrowing under 5 years","detail":"The council's borrowing maturity profile has shifted to be entirely long-dated, with zero borrowing under 5 years and 94% over 10 years, compared to permitted limits that would have allowed a balanced spread across all maturity buckets from under 1 year upwards. This concentrates all refinancing risk into future years.","category":"borrowing","matters":"Lenders assess maturity profile to evaluate refinancing risk; a portfolio with no short-term buffer and nearly all debt over 10 years creates a refinancing cliff when those loans mature, with no diversification across maturity dates to spread the risk","figures":"Under 1 year: 40% permitted, 0% actual; 2\u20135 years: 50% permitted, 0% actual; over 10 years: 100% permitted, 94% actual","quote":"Under 1 Year 40% 0%, 2 Years to 5 Years 50% 0%, Over 10 Years 100% 94%","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-30","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Appendix 2 - Prudential and Treasury Management Indicators 2025/26","paper_url":"https://democracy.gedling.gov.uk/documents/s45873/45873.pdf","headline":"Gross debt came in at \u00a310.8m, approximately half the \u00a321.2m forecast","detail":"The council's maximum gross debt was \u00a310.8m against an original forecast of \u00a321.2m\u2014approximately 51% of the anticipated level. The operational boundary for external borrowing was similarly constrained, at \u00a310.8m against an authorised limit of \u00a323m, indicating the council borrowed substantially less than planned.","category":"borrowing","matters":"Underborrowing relative to forecast could signal capital programme slippage or reduced ambition, or prudent cash management; coupled with financing costs doubling, it suggests interest rates on new or refinanced debt were significantly higher than forecast","figures":"\u00a321,226,000 (forecast gross debt) to \u00a310,811,577 (actual); borrowing operational boundary \u00a322,000,000 (forecast) to \u00a310,811,577 (actual)","quote":"Maximum Gross Debt 21,226,000\u00a3           10,811,577\u00a3","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-30","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Appendix 2 - Prudential and Treasury Management Indicators 2025/26","paper_url":"https://democracy.gedling.gov.uk/documents/s45873/45873.pdf","headline":"Financing costs ratio doubled from 2.21% to 4.62%, showing sharp deterioration in debt affordability","detail":"The council's debt service costs increased dramatically as a proportion of net revenue stream, nearly doubling from the forecast of 2.21% made in March 2025 to an actual 4.62% by year-end. This represents a material deterioration in the affordability of the council's debt burden despite lower overall borrowing.","category":"borrowing","matters":"Lenders use this ratio to assess whether a council's revenue can sustain its debt service; a near-doubling indicates debt service is now consuming much more revenue headroom, leaving less capacity to absorb financial shocks","figures":"2.21% (forecast) to 4.62% (actual)","quote":"Ratio of Financing Costs to Net Revenue Stream-Services 2.21% 4.62%","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-30","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Appendix 6 - Carry Forward Requests 2025-26, 25/06/2026 Cabinet","paper_url":"https://democracy.gedling.gov.uk/documents/s45869/45869.pdf","headline":"Capital programme delivered less than half planned budget with widespread project delays.","detail":"Only \u00a3957,524 of \u00a31,948,300 (49%) was spent in 2025-26. Vehicle Replacement Programme delayed by supply backlog, Jackie Bells Play Area delayed by contractor issues, Ambition Arnold Front Street awaiting contract signature. Total carry-forward of \u00a31,022,500 represents 52% of the approved budget.","category":"capital","matters":"Low capital delivery rate and delays across the portfolio indicate procurement or execution challenges that could affect the council's ability to deliver planned investment.","figures":"Total budget \u00a31,948,300; actual spend \u00a3957,524 (49%); total carry forward \u00a31,022,500","quote":"Project underway. Orders placed but delays due to backlog","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-30","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Appendix 6 - Carry Forward Requests 2025-26, 25/06/2026 Cabinet","paper_url":"https://democracy.gedling.gov.uk/documents/s45869/45869.pdf","headline":"Essential fire safety project overspent beyond budget, with shortfall covered from contingency reserve.","detail":"Fire door replacement project received contractor bids exceeding the \u00a3125,900 approved budget. An additional \u00a327,400 was required for essential H&S compliance works. The council deployed its unspent Asset Management Fund to cover the gap, resulting in a carry-forward request of \u00a3153,300.","category":"overspend","matters":"A mandatory safety project that overran reduces the council's contingency buffer and signals either estimation risk or market pressures that could affect future capital projects.","figures":"Original approved budget \u00a3125,900; additional requirement \u00a327,400; carry forward requested \u00a3153,300","quote":"Bids higher than budget envelope, essential H&S compliance works an additional \u00a327,400 required. Unspent Asset Management Fund budget has been utilised.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-06-26"},"name":"Gedling","findings_total":79,"news_drafts_total":3}}